# Cue: `[subject-id]` was modified — inflection?

## The Change
[What moved, in one paragraph: which commit(s), what changed in the subject,
and why the subject is reasoned-from — a definition surface, or its fan-in.
`mdllm touchpoints [subject-id]` lists what depends on it.]

## The Walk
[One line per dependant — `mdllm cues . --staged --raise` prefills the declared
and literal tiers; `mdllm touchpoints [subject-id]` lists the same. Mark each:
`consistent` (holds as written), `revised` (a restatement-level edit in this
commit — say what), `ruling` (the operator's answer, in their words, to a
question you could not settle: a change of meaning, a contradiction). Add a
line for any conceptual residue you find — a thing that reasons about the
subject without naming it. (`change-reconciliation.md` → The Walk Runs On
Detection.)]

## The Answer
[`inflection` when any line is revised or ruled; `not-inflection` when every
line held. This section is the walk's reasoning; `verdict_reason` above is its
one-line receipt. An unattended run leaves this open and writes its proposed
revisions here.]
